; Format: ini
; =====================================================================================
;  Wakes — Plaits Engine Stack Configuration
; =====================================================================================
;
;  Mutable Instruments Plaits is a Eurorack macro-oscillator module created by Émilie Gillet,
;  and its code comprises the audible portion of Wakes! Plaits has 24 sound engines. Its custom
;  firmware community has created many more over the years. Wakes currently features the originals.
;  This CNFG file determines the Plaits sound engines you want to include in your engine stack.
;  T2 and T3 step through the slots in the order shown below, skipping empty slots or unused lines.
;  Wakes starts on the first filled slot. You'll return to that slot when you Rip Out The Cables.
;
;  - LIST FORMAT:
;      N  = engine-name          ; <glyph>
;
;  - 16 default slots, with a maximum of 24. Each slot has its own glyph which flashes when selected.
;    Glyphs are shown after the ; on each line. The glyph belongs to the SLOT, not to the engine
;    in that slot. Moving an engine moves it to that slot's glyph.
;  - To include an engine, paste its name directly from the ENGINES section below.
;    Each engine can be used once.
;  - Leave a slot empty (or delete its line) to skip it.
;  - This file is the whole stack: a slot that is not listed here is empty.
;  - Engines that are not in the stack will still be usable if a PRST uses them.
;    You'll know an engine is not in your stack by a flashing glyph across all four face LEDs.
;  - If Wakes can't use this file (a misspelled engine, an engine used twice, or no engines at
;    all), it ignores the whole file and plays the 16 built-in engines. The log says which line.
;
;  Remember: in ini files, text following a ; or a # is a comment.

[engines]
1  = virtual-analog          ; ●○○○
2  = waveshaping             ; ●●○○
3  = 2-op-FM                 ; ●●●○
4  = grain-formant           ; ●●●●
5  = additive                ; ○●●●
6  = wavetable               ; ○○●●
7  = chords                  ; ○○○●
8  = speech                  ; ○●○○
9  = swarm                   ; ○○●○
10 = filtered-noise          ; ●○○●
11 = particle                ; ○●●○
12 = string                  ; ●○●●
13 = modal                   ; ●●○●
14 = bass-drum               ; ●○●○
15 = snare-drum              ; ○●○●
16 = hi-hat                  ; ○○○○
17 =                         ; ◐◐◐◐
18 =                         ; ○◐◐○
19 =                         ; ◐○○◐
20 =                         ; ○◐○◐
21 =                         ; ◐○◐○
22 =                         ; ○◐◐◐
23 =                         ; ○○○◐
24 =                         ; ○◐○○


; =====================================================================================
;  ENGINES
; =====================================================================================
;
;  This section contains a micro-manual for each Plaits engine Wakes can play, including
;  engine names to copy from and paste above.
;  Faders: F1 is always FREQ, but F2, F3 and F4 each have engine-unique parameters.
;  The signals offered on the AUX output also differ between engines.
;  Most engine parameters are unipolar. For engines where some parameters are bipolar,
;  they're indicated below.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  virtual-analog                                                      (default slot 1)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Two analog-style oscillators mixed together: a variable square and a variable saw.
;    F2 TIMB       the square: narrow pulse -> full square -> hard-sync formants
;    F3 MORP       the saw: triangle -> saw, with a notch that widens
;    F4 HARM       detune between the two oscillators
;    AUX           two hard-synced waveforms added together, shaped by MORP
;  Bipolar parameters: F2, F4.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  waveshaping                                                         (default slot 2)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A triangle wave through a waveshaper and a wavefolder.
;    F2 TIMB       how hard the wavefolder folds
;    F3 MORP       asymmetry of the waveform
;    F4 HARM       the waveshaper's curve
;    AUX           the same, through a different wavefolder curve
;  Bipolar parameters: F4.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  2-op-FM                                                             (default slot 3)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Two sine operators, one modulating the other's phase.
;    F2 TIMB       modulation index: how bright the tone is
;    F3 MORP       feedback: one operator modulating its own phase or the other's
;    F4 HARM       frequency ratio between the two operators
;    AUX           a sub-oscillator
;  Bipolar parameters: F3.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  grain-formant                                                       (default slot 4)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Vocal-like formants made from windowed sine grains.
;    F2 TIMB       formant frequency
;    F3 MORP       formant width and shape
;    F4 HARM       frequency ratio between the two formants
;    AUX           filtered waveforms imitated with windowed sines
;  Bipolar parameters: F4.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  additive                                                            (default slot 5)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A sum of harmonics whose levels follow one or more bumps in the spectrum.
;    F2 TIMB       which harmonic is loudest -- a little like a filter cutoff
;    F3 MORP       bump shape: flat and wide -> peaked and narrow
;    F4 HARM       how many bumps the spectrum has, starting from one
;    AUX           only the harmonics a drawbar organ has

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  wavetable                                                           (default slot 6)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Banks of single-cycle waves laid out in a grid.
;    F2 TIMB       wavetable row: the waves are sorted dark to bright
;    F3 MORP       wavetable column: select shape families
;    F4 HARM       which bank (from the middle down, TIMB and MORP are interpolated)
;    AUX           a low-fi, 5-bit version

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  chords                                                              (default slot 7)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Four-note chords played by a string-machine ensemble or a wavetable scan.
;    F2 TIMB       chord voicing - inversion and transposition
;    F3 MORP       waveform: string-machine sounds below the middle, wavetable above
;    F4 HARM       chord types: oct, 5, sus4, m, m7, m9, m11, 69, M9, M7, M
;    AUX           the chord's isolated root note

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  speech                                                              (default slot 8)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A collection of speech synth algorithms: formant filters, SAM, LPC vowels and words.
;    F2 TIMB       size of the speaker, from Daleks to chipmunks (Émilie's wording lol)
;    F3 MORP       which vowel, phoneme or word segment
;    F4 HARM       the method: formants -> SAM -> LPC vowels, then banks of LPC words
;    AUX           the raw voice source, pre-filtering

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  swarm                                                               (default slot 9)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Eight saw-like grains, each slightly detuned: a cloud of voices.
;    F2 TIMB       how many grains per second
;    F3 MORP       grain length and overlap; at the top they run into each other
;    F4 HARM       how far each grain's pitch wanders
;    AUX           the same cloud made of sine waves

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  filtered-noise                                                     (default slot 10)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Clocked noise through a resonant filter.
;    F2 TIMB       the noise's clock rate
;    F3 MORP       filter resonance
;    F4 HARM       filter type: low-pass -> band-pass -> high-pass
;    AUX           two band-pass filters, as far apart as HARM sets
;  Bipolar parameters: F4.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  particle                                                           (default slot 11)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Random impulses ringing through filters: rain, crackle, droplets.
;    F2 TIMB       how dense the particles are
;    F3 MORP       below centre: reverberating all-pass network, above it: resonant
;                  band-pass filters
;    F4 HARM       how random each particle's pitch is
;    AUX           the raw impulses (dust)
;  Bipolar parameters: F3.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  string                                                             (default slot 12)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A plucked or bowed string, modelled physically. Two strings take turns, so a new note
;  can ring while the last one fades.
;    F2 TIMB       how bright the excitation is (and how dense, while it drones)
;    F3 MORP       decay time
;    F4 HARM       inharmonicity: dispersive at the bottom, stiff at the top, and
;                  harmonic in a small zone about a quarter of the way up
;    AUX           the raw excitation

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  modal                                                              (default slot 13)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A struck resonator: bells, bars, plates, membranes.
;    F2 TIMB       how bright the excitation is (and how dense, while it drones)
;    F3 MORP       decay time
;    F4 HARM       the material: how inharmonic the resonator is
;    AUX           the raw excitation

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  bass-drum                                                          (default slot 14)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  An analog-style kick.
;    F2 TIMB       brightness
;    F3 MORP       decay time
;    F4 HARM       how sharp the attack is, and how much overdrive
;    AUX           a different kick: a frequency-modulated triangle shaped into a sine

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  snare-drum                                                         (default slot 15)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  An analog-style snare: tuned drum modes and noise.
;    F2 TIMB       balance between the drum's modes
;    F3 MORP       decay time
;    F4 HARM       balance between the drum and the noise
;    AUX           a different snare: two frequency-modulated sines and high-passed noise

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  hi-hat                                                             (default slot 16)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A metallic hi-hat: square oscillators ring-modulating each other, plus noise.
;    F2 TIMB       high-pass filter cutoff
;    F3 MORP       decay time
;    F4 HARM       balance between the metal and the noise
;    AUX           a different hi-hat: three pairs of ring-modulated squares, cleaner

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  VA-VCF                                                    (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A classic subtractive voice: an analog-style oscillator into a resonant filter.
;    F2 TIMB       filter cutoff
;    F3 MORP       waveform, and how much sub-oscillator
;    F4 HARM       resonance and character: a gentle 24 dB/oct filter below the middle,
;                  a harsh 12 dB/oct one above
;    AUX           the high-pass output
;  Bipolar parameters: F3, F4.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  phase-distortion                                          (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A sine whose phase is bent by a second oscillator: Casio-style tones.
;    F2 TIMB       how much distortion
;    F3 MORP       how asymmetric the distortion is
;    F4 HARM       the distorting oscillator's frequency
;    AUX           the same with the carrier running free: phase modulation

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  wave-terrain                                              (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A point circling over a 3D surface; the height under it is the sound.
;    F2 TIMB       the size of the circle
;    F3 MORP       where the circle sits on the surface
;    F4 HARM       which surface
;    AUX           the height used to bend the phase of a sine instead
;  Bipolar parameters: F3.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  string-machine                                            (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A vintage string ensemble playing chords, through a chorus and a filter.
;    F2 TIMB       chorus and filter amount
;    F3 MORP       waveform
;    F4 HARM       chord
;    AUX           part of the chord (mostly the 2nd and 4th voices)
;  Bipolar parameters: F2.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  chiptune                                                  (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  An 8-bit game console: pulse waves playing chords and arpeggios.
;    F2 TIMB       arpeggio pattern, or chord inversion
;    F3 MORP       pulse width, and sync
;    F4 HARM       chord
;    AUX           the console's triangle voice

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  6-op-FM-A        6-op-FM-B        6-op-FM-C               (not in the default stack)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Three banks A, B and C, each containing 32 six-operator FM patches in the style of a DX7.
;    F2 TIMB       modulator levels
;    F3 MORP       stretches the envelopes and the modulation ("time travel")
;    F4 HARM       Bank patch selection
;    AUX           the same as OUT
;  Bipolar parameters: F3.
